# THOOGUDEEPA ENTERPRISE SUITE — MASTER ARCHITECTURE & CODING RULES
# Permanent memory and context for Cursor, Cline, Copilot, and LLM Agents.
# Read and follow these rules strictly before modifying or creating any code in this repository.

# ==============================================================================
# 1. RESTAURANT DOMAIN & BUSINESS MODEL
# ==============================================================================
# Brand: Thoogudeepa Donne Biryani Mane
# Concept: Authentic military-style high-volume restaurant in Bengaluru.
# Physical layout: Exactly 34 tables and 133 seats partitioned into 5 zones:
#   - Express / Couple Hall: Tables T-01 to T-04 (2 seats each = 8 seats)
#   - Main Dining Hall: Tables T-05 to T-14 (3 seats each = 30 seats)
#   - Family Section: Tables T-15 to T-24 (4 seats each = 40 seats)
#   - Courtyard Garden: Tables T-25 to T-29 (5 seats each = 25 seats)
#   - Grand Feast Hall: Tables T-30 to T-34 (6 seats each = 30 seats)
#   TOTAL CAPACITY: 133 Seats across 34 Tables.

# ==============================================================================
# 2. STEWARD IDENTIFICATION & PIN CONVENTIONS
# ==============================================================================
# Quick Login Steward PINs:
#   - 1111: Captain Ramesh (Assigned: Express / Couple Hall & Section A)
#   - 2222: Captain Suresh (Assigned: Main Dining Hall & Section B)
#   - 3333: Captain Nayana (Assigned: Family Section & Section C)
#   - 4444: Captain Vennela (Assigned: Courtyard Garden & Grand Feast Hall)
#   - 1234: Universal Floor Captain / General Manager override PIN

# ==============================================================================
# 3. FINANCIAL & TAXATION RULES
# ==============================================================================
# GST Rate: Flat 5% GST added on top of food & beverage subtotal.
# Calculation formula:
#   const tax = Math.round(subtotal * 0.05);
#   const total = subtotal + tax;
# Never alter this rounding formula. It is enforced across all API routes and UI components.

# Identifier Formatting Standards:
#   - Orders:      `ORD-${cleanTable}-S${seatNumber}-${Date.now().toString().slice(-6)}`
#   - KOT Tickets: `KOT-${cleanTable}-${Date.now().toString().slice(-4)}`
#   - Pings:       `PING-${cleanTable}-S${seatNumber}-${Date.now().toString().slice(-4)}`
#   - Payments:    `PAY-${Date.now()}-${Math.floor(1000 + Math.random() * 9000)}`
#   - Invoices:    `INV-${cleanTable}-${Date.now().toString().slice(-6)}`
#   - Bank UTR:    12-digit authentic Indian bank RRN (e.g. `4281${Math.floor(10000000 + Math.random() * 90000000)}`)

# ==============================================================================
# 4. STATE MANAGEMENT & ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS
# ==============================================================================
# Single Source of Cross-Portal Truth:
#   `store/useSharedBridge.ts`
#
# Rules for Store Interaction:
#   1. Tables (`tables`), KDS Tickets (`kdsTickets`), Customer Pings (`pings`),
#      Shift Statistics (`shiftStats`), and 86 Stock (`inventory86`) are managed
#      exclusively by `useSharedBridge`.
#   2. Individual portal stores (`useWaiterStore`, `useKitchenStore`) MUST NOT maintain
#      duplicate state arrays for tables or tickets. They must export and use selectors
#      pointing to `useSharedBridge` (e.g., `useTables`, `useKDSTickets`, `useKitchenReadyItems`).
#   3. Cross-tab synchronization is powered by localStorage broadcast events. Always maintain
#      the window storage event listener and rehydration guards.
#   4. Multi-Table Merge Logic:
#      - Master table maintains `mergeGroupPeers?: string[]` containing all peer table numbers.
#      - Slave tables hold `mergedWith?: string` pointing to master.
#      - Pre-merge caches (`preMergeBill`, `preMergeGuests`, `preMergeStatus`, `preMergeCapacity`)
#        must be stored on slave tables to ensure 100% lossless unmerging.

# ==============================================================================
# 5. TABLET COCKPIT & UI SCALING INVARIANTS
# ==============================================================================
# Target Canvas Dimensions:
#   Width: 1194px | Height: 834px (Standard iPad / Android POS landscape viewport).
# Scaled via dynamic CSS transform in `app/waiter/tablet/page.tsx`.
#
# CRITICAL MODAL CENTERING INVARIANT:
#   Because the parent container uses CSS `transform: scale(...)`, any modal using
#   `fixed top-1/2 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2` will suffer severe
#   visual coordinate displacement.
#   All modals (Shift, Merge, Split, Settle) MUST use the full-screen flex wrapper:
#   `<div className="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center p-4 bg-black/60 backdrop-blur-xs">`
#   Never revert modals to coordinate translation transforms.

# ==============================================================================
# 6. DATABASE SCHEMA & SUPABASE INTERACTION
# ==============================================================================
# Production Database: Supabase PostgreSQL
# Canonical Tables:
#   1. `tables` (number, section, capacity, status, guest_count, current_bill, server_name, kot_count, merged_with)
#   2. `table_seats` (table_number, seat_number, status, active_order_id, device_token)
#   3. `orders` (id, table_number, seat_number, guest_name, items, subtotal, tax, total, total_amount, status, source)
#   4. `order_items` (id, order_id, table_number, seat_number, name, quantity, price, unit_price, total_price, stage, prep_mode)
#   5. `kds_tickets` (id, order_id, table_number, seat_number, server_name, status, source, items)
#   6. `payments` (id, order_id, table_number, seat_number, amount, payment_method, gateway_ref, bank_utr, status, confirmed_at)
#   7. `pings` (id, table_number, seat_number, type, guest_name, message, status)
#   8. `menu_86` (id, name, category, is_86, prep_delay_minutes)
#
# Order Stage Stepping:
#   `PLACED` -> `PREP` -> `PLATED` -> `SERVED`
# Ticket Transition:
#   `NEW` -> `PREP` -> `READY` -> `COMPLETED`

# ==============================================================================
# 7. CODE HYGIENE & PRODUCTION SAFETY
# ==============================================================================
# 1. Zero AI traces: Never introduce words like 'Claude', 'Gemini', 'GPT', 'AI generated',
#    or temporary prompt commentary into source files.
# 2. Strict Type Safety: Run `npm run type-check` (`tsc --noEmit`) before committing. Zero errors allowed.
# 3. Test Matrix Integrity: Run `npm run test:waiter:matrix`. All 93+ test assertions must pass 100%.
# 4. Clean Build: Run `npm run build`. Next.js build must finish with exit code 0.
